From: blockdomains OHOS port
Subject: [PATCH] HarmonyOS: avoid sockaddr_storage redefinition from linux/socket.h

On HarmonyOS (musl libc + Linux uapi headers), <linux/netfilter.h> pulls in
<linux/in.h> which includes <linux/socket.h>; that header re-defines
struct sockaddr_storage which musl's <sys/socket.h> (reached earlier via
<netinet/in.h>) has already defined. The same conflict would be re-triggered
by <libnetfilter_queue/libnetfilter_queue.h> through its
<linux/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.h> -> <linux/netlink.h> chain.

Fix: define _UAPI_LINUX_SOCKET_H before the first Linux uapi network header
so <linux/socket.h> is skipped entirely, and supply the
__kernel_sa_family_t typedef it would otherwise provide. This mirrors the
guard already used by the babeld 1.13.1 port in this repository
(archives/b/babeld/1.13.1/patches/0001-harmoneyos-fix-sockaddr-storage-redefinition.patch).

Verified on-device with clang 15 (aarch64-linux-ohos, SDK sysroot):
unpatched include chain fails with "error: redefinition of 'sockaddr_storage'";
patched chain and all three sources compile cleanly.
---
--- a/src/blockdomains.c
+++ b/src/blockdomains.c
@@ -8,6 +8,12 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
+/* HarmonyOS: linux/netfilter.h (via linux/in.h) and the libnetfilter_queue
+   header chain (via linux/netlink.h) both include linux/socket.h, which
+   re-defines struct sockaddr_storage already defined by sys/socket.h.
+   Define the needed type and skip the header. */
+#define _UAPI_LINUX_SOCKET_H
+typedef unsigned short __kernel_sa_family_t;
 #include <linux/netfilter.h>            /* for NF_ACCEPT */
 #include <libnetfilter_queue/libnetfilter_queue.h>
 
